meta {
  name: 12 Repeat Sample
  type: http
  seq: 12
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/accession/order-samples/{{sampleId}}/repeat
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "repeatReason": "QC Failure",
    "notes": "Re-collection requested"
  }
}

tests {
  test("transition applied (or rejected by the state machine)", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.be.oneOf([200, 201, 422]);
  });
}

docs {
  Repeat — **Acquired / Halt / Error → Repeat**. `repeatReason` is **required**
  (branch-configured list), recorded as the history reason.

  Repeat of a receiving branch's accepted COPY sends the test back to its sender
  (report reset, see Transfer - Repeat).
  **Cancelled order:** once the receiving branch has ACCEPTED its copy, the copy
  holds typed results, so it can no longer be sent back to the sender - refused
  with 422 `SAMPLE_ORDER_CANCELLED` (a group call with `skipInvalid` skips it with
  that reason) and nothing changes; Store then Discard stay open. Before Accept
  (transfer only Received) the receiving branch can still Reject / Repeat.
}
